# Quality bar

A short is a **vertical 1080×1920** piece. `kind=drama` is a **short story** (bible faces, motion). `kind=news` and `kind=knowledge` are **ảnh ghép** (editorial stills + Ken Burns), not character cinema.

**Must**

- 1080×1920 @ 30fps, VO + karaoke ASS, duration = probed audio.
- One still per scene; 1–3 shots share `still_id`. Drama faces come from the Character Bible passport, not a new description. Drama uses close-up beat lenses and I2V when keyed. News/knowledge stills are editorial and **match that beat's VO**; no on-camera bible faces; Ken Burns on medium/wide so screenshots stay in frame.
- Shots follow beat lenses (exact pairs in `docs/REQUIREMENTS.md` §6). Drama: hook push-in → conflict tight → rising pan → twist punch-in → ending pull-out.
- Image: photographic stills when Pollinations is on. Drama compact prompt leads with **ONLY on-camera ids**. News/knowledge compact prompt leads with editorial still, no soap-opera couple. Kontext from the passport **URL** on drama only. Fail the still rather than mix stick figures. Inserts: no full-body crowd.
- Motion: drama prefers I2V when `HF_TOKEN` or Pollinations pollen exists. Editorial collage stays Ken Burns. Never call Ken Burns I2V.
- Motion prompt = camera + action only. No VO text in image/video prompts.

**Must not**

- One image per sentence. Pexels as the picture. Fun-fact / explainer beats **in drama**. Bending a **custom** prompt into the default humiliation shape, or ignoring the user's characters in **default** mode. Knowledge may narrate a single claim, never a random trivia listicle. News must cover the article ending, not stop at the first conflict.
- HyperFrames HTML templates. Hardcoding Kling/Veo/OpenMontage in the planner. Forking those repos.
- Shipping a still as if people were animated. Write `render/motion.json` (`kenburns` | `i2v` | `mixed`).

When quality is “not OK”, fix identity (bible → kontext) or motion (I2V keys / Ken Burns lenses). Do not add a new product surface. Do not turn news/knowledge into drama.
